kdrm-core: shared DRM core following Linux v7.2.3 DRM semantics
================================================================

Layer: reusable component. Kernel operations are supplied by drm-kapi.

License: every file in this component is MIT-licensed (see LICENSE-MIT).
The copyright lines in LICENSE-MIT are retained from the MIT/X11-licensed
Linux DRM sources whose behavior these modules follow.

Correspondence with Linux:

- Function modules (`*_upstream.rs`) are named after the Linux DRM source
  file whose behavior they implement. `// upstream:` comments name the
  corresponding Linux function so that semantics can be reviewed against
  Linux v7.2.3.
- Type modules (`*_types.rs`) define C-layout structures that match the
  Linux v7.2.3 x86_64 definitions. Compile-time assertions pin the internal
  sizes and offsets the core relies on for the supported 64-bit
  little-endian targets. They are not user-ABI or hardware validation.

Not part of this component: firmware framebuffer and fbdev, Intel display
and GT drivers, DRM bridge, and DP MST.

Test fixtures: every EDID used by the host tests is built in code
(`drm_edid_upstream.rs`, `tests` module). No Linux test data is copied.
